title: Presidential Veto
subtitle: [+ president +] vetoes the [+ veto_reason +]
tags: event
new-page: true
view-if: veto > 0 and president_party = "dem"
on-arrival: {!

    Q.veto = 0;

    if (Q.veto_reason == "Civil Rights Act") {
        Q.civil_rights_act_passed = 0;
        Q.freedmen_rep -= 3;
        Q.radical_strength -= 3;
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 1;
        Q.civil_rights -= 5;
    }
    if (Q.veto_reason == "Tenure of Office Act") {
        Q.impeachment_ready = 0;
        Q.tenure_act = 0;
        Q.radical_strength -= 3;
        Q.radical_dissent += 1;
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 1;
    }
    if (Q.veto_reason == "Military Reconstruction Act") {
        Q.Radical_plan = 0;
        Q.Johnson_plan = 1;
        Q.occupation = 0;
        Q.radical_strength -= 3;
        Q.moderate_strength -= 2;
        Q.freedmen_rep -= 2;
        Q.kkk_strength += 5;
        Q.kkk_militancy += 0.2;

        for (let state of Q.southern_states) {
            let loyalty = Q[state + "_loyalty"] || 0;
            let equality = Q[state + "_raceEqualitySupport"] || 0;
            let score = Math.round((loyalty * 0.55) + (equality * 0.45));
            Q[state + "_reconstructionScore"] = score;
            Q[state + "_canReadmit"] = score >= 20 ? 1 : 0;
        }
    }
!}

= [+ president +] vetoes the [+ veto_reason +]

President [+ president +] has vetoed the [+ veto_reason +], declaring it "an unconstitutional assault on states' rights and an invitation to tyranny."

<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> are outraged. They see this as further proof that [+ president +] is siding with the <span style="color: #002765;">**Redeemers**</span> and obstructing the goals of Reconstruction. <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> are split on the issue.

With the Radical base demanding action and the President daring Congress to respond, the veto becomes a moment of truth.

- @override: Attempt to override the veto.
- @stand_down: Let the veto stand, for now.

@override
subtitle: Requires 2/3 in both chambers.
choose-if: house_majority = 3 and sen_majority = 3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if house_majority < 3: We lack the supermajority in the House needed to override. ?][? if sen_majority < 3: We lack the supermajority in the Senate needed to override. ?]
on-arrival: {!

    if (Q.veto_reason == "Civil Rights Act") {
        Q.civil_rights_act_passed = 1;
        Q.freedmen_rep += 3;
        Q.radical_strength += 3;
        Q.moderate_dissent += 3;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
        Q.liberal_dissent += 1;
        Q.civil_rights += 3;
    }
    if (Q.veto_reason == "Tenure of Office Act") {
        Q.impeachment_ready = 1;
        Q.tenure_act = 2;
        Q.radical_strength += 3;
        Q.radical_dissent -= 1;
        Q.moderate_dissent += 1;
    }
    if (Q.veto_reason == "Military Reconstruction Act") {
        Q.Radical_plan = 1;
        Q.Johnson_plan = 0;
        Q.occupation = 2;
        Q.radical_strength += 3;
        Q.moderate_strength += 2;
        Q.freedmen_rep += 2;
        for (let state of Q.southern_states) {
            Q[state + "_admitted"] = 0;
        }
    }

    Q.veto_reason = "";
!}

We move swiftly to override the President's veto. With overwhelming support in Congress, the law is enacted anyway. [+ president +]'s influence shrinks and our <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical**</span> base cheers.

@stand_down
subtitle: Political caution.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.moderate_strength += 2;
    Q.radical_dissent += 4;
    Q.freedmen_rep -= 2;
    Q.veto_reason = "";
!}

We are forced to back down as [+ president +] has won this time. <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> defend our decision as strategic but to many, it looks like cowardice. The veto holds.